## VS Code — ignore user preferences but keep project launch/task config
.vscode/*
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

## Secrets and environment-specific config
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.*.json
!appsettings.json
# The API's Development overrides ARE committed and are load-bearing: they hold no secrets
# (empty App Insights connection string, the shared Key Vault URI, Features:AllowAnonymousWrites)
# and both test host fixtures run as Development, so they inherit this file. The blanket rules
# above matched it while git kept honouring it only because it was already tracked — this
# negation makes the intent explicit so a delete-and-re-add cannot silently drop it.
!src/PoLocalCompare.Api/appsettings.Development.json

